<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Disco cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Disco cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING Barings analyst Tadd Chessen has downgraded his rating for Argentine supermarket chain Disco SA to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- In a July 8 report, he said the downgrade was based on Disco's current price appreciation.</p>
<p>-- He revised his June 1998 price target to $46 per American Depositary Receipt, implying an appreciation of 6.7 percent from current levels.</p>
<p>-- The ADRs closed Tuesday at 43.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
